  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following sequence of reactions:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/TOgY2uNT_YZiCreqYgUOPImIksWaQvnE2GsX9Yp-mNY.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\n11.25 mg of chlorobenzene will produce __________ $\\times 10^{-1} \\mathrm{mg}$ of product B .\n(Consider the reactions result in complete conversion.)\n[Given molar mass of $\\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{H}, \\mathrm{O}, \\mathrm{N}$ and Cl as $12,1,16,14$ and $35.5 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ respectively]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "93",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/F1e799PZr4Y4O6MiVN1S0ptdKC2Usn5YXYlhSfeQCdo.original.fullsize.png\"><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4ebdZIKNISpOEWQlp8p98MHVOjANeE1tyhbYFvvrDYI.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{11.25 \\times 10^{-3}}{112.5}=\\frac{x \\times 10^{-1} \\times 10^{-3}}{93} \\\\ & x \\times 10^{-1}=93 \\times 0.1 \\\\ & x=93 \\mathrm{mg}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
